    "structured_output": {
      "summary": "Partial result. I implemented the S2 Theorem 3.7 cumulative recurrence with exact integers (code/recurrence.py) and checked it three ways: it reproduces all 45 values of S1 Table 1, it matches direct enumeration of every preference list for n≤7 (823,543 lists at n=7), and it matches the S1 formula (4) permutation products for n≤9 (25 checks, data/verify_small.json). In the preliminary exact computation, every row with n≤30 is unimodal. In the sampled rows n=80, 100, 120, 150 and 200, log-concavity fails around k≈n/2, before the peak. The full-row analysis up to N=500 (code/analyze.py) failed: after 156.8 s of recurrence computation, gzip.open(mtime=0) raised a TypeError, so no data files or tables were produced. I have fixed the code but not rerun it. The criterion-3 table of all rows for N≥150 therefore does not exist yet. Unimodality has been checked only for n≤30.",
      "used_sources": [
        "TK-01M2S813V9QTR85ACN7F9RA8DV",
        "source:선행연구와-시작-자료.md",
        "source:published-counts.json",
        "source:verify_reference.py",
        "context:goal"
      ],
      "questions": [],
      "outcome": "partial",
      "report": "## What was done\n1. **Recurrence implementation** (code/recurrence.py): A_{0,ℓ}=1 and A_{n,ℓ}=Σ_j C(n−1,j)·min(j+1,ℓ+1)·A_{j,ℓ}·A_{n−1−j,ℓ} (S2 Theorem 3.7). When n−1≤ℓ, A_{n,ℓ}=(n+1)^{n−1}. b_{n,ℓ}=A_{n,ℓ}−A_{n,ℓ−1} with A_{n,−1}=0. All judgements use Python int only. Timings: N=150 about 2.3 s, N=300 about 13 s, N=500 about 157 s.\n2. **Independent cross-checks** (code/verify_small.py → data/verify_small.json, all_passed=true, 25 checks):\n   - It reproduces all 45 values for n=1..9 in S1 Table 1.\n   - It agrees with S1 formula (4), Σ_σ∏min(ℓ+1,r_i(σ)), for n=1..9.\n   - It agrees with direct enumeration of every list in [1..n]^n (a parking simulation) for n=1..7.\n   - The last two methods do not use the recurrence code.\n   - Rerun: from the workspace root, `python -B code/verify_small.py` (about 5 s).\n3. **Preliminary exact observations** (one run up to N=200; not saved as a judgement file):\n   - **n=1..30:** the difference-sign pattern is '+^c −^(n−1−c)', so every row is unimodal and has no ties. The peaks c(n) are 0,0,1,1,1,2,2,3,3,4,4,5,6,6,7,8,9,9,10,11,12,13,14,14,15,16,17,18,19,20. Every row is log-concave.\n   - **argmax of the sampled rows:** n=40:28, 50:37, 60:45, 80:63, 100:81, 120:99, 150:126, 200:172.\n   - **Sampled rows were not checked for unimodality:** for n>30 I printed only the first and last parts of each pattern.\n   - **Log-concavity failures (b_k² < b_{k−1}b_{k+1}):** n=80 at k=40; n=100 at k=50..52; n=120 at k=59..65; n=150 from k=74; n=200 from k=99. There were no failures in the samples with n≤60.\n   - **Peak position guess:** n−c≈2√n is only a hypothesis from a few samples.\n   - **Implication:** log-concavity and ratio monotonicity cannot serve as the strengthening hypothesis for an induction over all n. A log-concavity failure is not a unimodality violation, so it is not a refutation of P.\n\n## Failure and current state\n- `python -B code/analyze.py 500 300` finished the recurrence computation (156.8 s) and then stopped with `TypeError: open() got an unexpected keyword argument 'mtime'` at line 91, `gzip.open(..., mtime=0)`. None of data/b_rows_n1-300.jsonl.gz, row_hashes.json, analysis.json or analysis_table.md was created.\n- I changed that call to gzip.GzipFile(fileobj=..., mode=\"wb\", compresslevel=9, mtime=0). I have not rerun it, so it is unverified.\n- code/shape_observations.py, which reads analysis.json, has been written but not run.\n- checkpoint.json records this state.\n\n## Completion criteria\n- 1. Satisfied.\n- 2. Satisfied.\n- 3. Not satisfied. Only rows n≤30 were judged.\n- 4. Partially satisfied: all rows n≤30 plus the sampled rows.\n- 5. No violation found; judged only for n≤30.\n- 6. Code and rerun commands exist. The large data files, their hashes and the report do not.",
      "knowledge": [
        {
          "kind": "observation",
          "title": "최대 변위 개수 점화식의 공개 값·전수 순회·식 (4) 교차 검증",
